 ## Overview
-DAVIGS is a plug-and-post appearance modeling method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that mitigates floaters and color distortions caused by appearance variations (e.g., daylight changes, ISP processing, local lighting) by transforming rendered images at the image level using 3D consistent features [S1]. Unlike coupled methods that manipulate Gaussian properties and slow rendering, or decoupled methods that only handle mild global variations, DAVIGS decouples global view-dependent appearance from local spatial changes, ensuring 3D consistency while maintaining real-time rendering speeds by discarding the appearance module after optimization [S1].
+DAVIGS is a plug-and-play appearance modeling method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that mitigates floaters and color distortions caused by appearance variations (e.g., daylight changes, ISP processing, local lighting) by transforming rendered images at the image level using 3D consistent features [S1]. Unlike coupled methods that manipulate Gaussian properties and slow rendering, or decoupled methods that only handle mild global variations, DAVIGS decouples global view-dependent appearance from local spatial changes, ensuring 3D consistency while maintaining real-time rendering speeds by discarding the appearance module after optimization [S1].
 
