 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** Optimization time is reduced by the cell-based query approach, which computes transformation matrices for cells rather than every pixel. Rendering speed is not compromised as the appearance module is discarded after optimization [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Additional memory is used for the multi-resolution hash grids and the MLP parameters. The global appearance embedding is small [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Additional memory is used for the multi-resolution hash grids and the MLP parameters [S1].
 *   **Strengths:** Plug-and-play, decouples global and local appearance variations, maintains real-time rendering speeds, ensures 3D consistency [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires depth map rendering for back-projection. Performance may degrade if depth estimation is inaccurate [S1].
+*   **Limitations:** Requires depth map rendering for back-projection [S1].
 *   **When to Use:** Scenes with significant appearance variations (e.g., daylight changes, local lighting changes) where coupled methods are too slow or decoupled methods fail to capture local variations [S1].
-*   **When Not to Use:** Scenes with minimal appearance variations where the overhead of the appearance module is not justified [S1].
 
